Install `maplibre-gl` (^4.x) and `@types/maplibre-gl`. Create a `Map` component in `frontend/src/components/Map.tsx` that initializes MapLibre with `VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL` from env (MapTiler/Stadia/Protomaps vector tiles). Implement:
- Map initialization with center/zoom from user's geolocation or default
- Click handler to set destination marker
- Display route polyline from match response (GeoJSON LineString)
- Show protest route overlays when conflicts exist
- Geocoding fallback for address input (via MapTiler/Nominatim if VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL provider supports it)

Store map instance in ref, expose methods to parent (setRoute, setMarkers). Use React.memo to prevent unnecessary re-renders. Add CSS for map container (100% height/width of parent). The component should gracefully handle missing `VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL` by showing a placeholder message.

Pseudo-code:
```tsx
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css'

const Map = ({ onDestinationSet, route, protestRoutes }) => {
  const mapRef = useRef<maplibregl.Map>()
  const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!containerRef.current || !VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL) return
    const map = new maplibregl.Map({
      container: containerRef.current,
      style: VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL,
      center: [lng, lat],
      zoom: 12
    })
    mapRef.current = map
    // Add click listener, add controls
    return () => map.remove()
  }, [])

  // Update route layer when route changes
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!mapRef.current || !route) return
    // Add/update GeoJSON source + layer for route
  }, [route])
}
```

Enhance `frontend/src/components/MatchPanel.tsx` (already exists as shell) to:
1. Accept current location (via geolocation API) and destination (from map click or text input)
2. Call `POST /api/protests/match` via the API client (`frontend/src/lib/api.ts`)
3. Display match results:
   - If no conflict: show primary route on map
   - If conflict: show protest details card (title, cause, goal, organizers with links, event date/time), explain why route conflicts, display suggested alternate route
   - Include "Add to Calendar" buttons (Google Calendar link + .ics download from response.calendar_links)
4. Handle loading/error states (show spinner during API call, error message on failure)
5. Bilingual UI using react-i18next (all labels translated)

Use existing types from `frontend/src/lib/types.ts` (Protest, MatchResponse). Style with CSS custom properties for theming. Show protest route overlay on map in contrasting color when conflict exists.

Pseudo-code:
```tsx
const MatchPanel = () => {
  const [origin, setOrigin] = useState<[number, number]>()
  const [destination, setDestination] = useState<[number, number]>()
  const [result, setResult] = useState<MatchResponse>()
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)
  const { t } = useTranslation()

  const handlePlanRoute = async () => {
    setLoading(true)
    const res = await api.matchRoute({ origin, destination })
    setResult(res)
    setLoading(false)
  }

  return (
    <div>
      <Map onDestinationSet={setDestination} route={result?.suggested_route} />
      {result?.conflict && (
        <ConflictCard protest={result.protest} calendarLinks={result.calendar_links} />
      )}
    </div>
  )
}
```

