      <a href={protest.calendarLinks.google}>Add to Google Calendar</a>
      <a href={`/api/protests/${id}/calendar.ics`} download>Download .ics</a>
    </div>
  )
}
```

Configure `vite-plugin-pwa` in `frontend/vite.config.ts` (already installed) to:
1. Cache app shell (HTML, CSS, JS) on install (precaching)
2. Runtime cache for API responses: `/api/protests`, `/api/protests/:id`, `/api/parking` (NetworkFirst strategy with 5min cache, fallback to cache when offline)
3. Cache map tiles from `VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL` domain (CacheFirst with 7-day expiration)
4. Exclude from cache: `/api/protests/match`, `/api/chips` (always require network for live data)
5. Update manifest.json with app name (bilingual), icons, theme color, start_url, display: standalone
6. Add "Update Available" prompt when new service worker detected

Generate 192x192 and 512x512 app icons. Use Workbox strategies via vite-plugin-pwa options.

Config example:
```ts
import { VitePWA } from 'vite-plugin-pwa'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    VitePWA({
      registerType: 'autoUpdate',
      manifest: {
        name: 'Protest Tracker',
        short_name: 'ProtestTracker',
        theme_color: '#000000',
        icons: [...]
      },
      workbox: {
        runtimeCaching: [
          {
            urlPattern: /^\/api\/protests(\/.+)?$/,
            handler: 'NetworkFirst',
            options: { cacheName: 'protests', expiration: { maxAgeSeconds: 300 } }
          },
          {
            urlPattern: /^https:\/\/(.*)\.maptiler\.com\/.+/,
            handler: 'CacheFirst',
            options: { cacheName: 'map-tiles', expiration: { maxEntries: 500, maxAgeSeconds: 604800 } }
          }
        ]
      }
    })
  ]
})
```

